    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d413">

                <pb facs="0484" n="366" xml:id="pg366"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00Sonora/309: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Morrow</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-03-16T12:00:00-05:00">March 16,
                    1929—noon</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>160. Following from Chihuahua: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“March 14, 5 p.m. Many Mexicans anxious avoid further bloodshed and
                            suggest that Ambassador Morrow offer his good offices to mediate
                            differences between Mexico and revolutionists. I have asked the opinion
                            of the leaders in Chihuahua and they would consider any decorous
                            propositions which the government of Mexico cares to offer to be
                            submitted to the supreme commander. Leaders would expect removal of
                            principal cause of the revolt.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Department has replied as follows through Ciudad Juarez: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Your March 14, 5 p.m. Unless directly instructed by the Department or
                            the Ambassador you will refrain from discussing with anybody the
                            question of mediation between the Federal Government and the
                            rebels.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Clark</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
